---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="AI BOM Copilot" sideBarActiveItemID="projects">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <a href="/projects" class="link link-hover text-sm opacity-70">← Back to Projects</a>
    <div class="mt-5 mb-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <span class="badge badge-secondary">PERSONAL BUILD</span>
      <span class="badge badge-outline">INTERACTIVE DEMO</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">AI BOM Copilot</h1>
    <p class="text-xl opacity-80 max-w-3xl">A component-sourcing workflow prototype that turns messy BOM inputs into structured rows and reviewable supplier candidates.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-6">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://ai-bom-demo.buwygfimb.workers.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Launch Live Demo ↗</a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://github.com/wantosleep3/ai-bom-Copilot" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View Source ↗</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 mb-9">
    <div class="card bg-base-200 p-4">
      <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide opacity-60">Built with</div>
      <div class="font-semibold mt-1">JavaScript · Cloudflare Workers</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card bg-base-200 p-4">
      <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide opacity-60">Core workflow</div>
      <div class="font-semibold mt-1">Normalize → Search → Review</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card bg-base-200 p-4">
      <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide opacity-60">Project status</div>
      <div class="font-semibold mt-1">Portfolio prototype</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="mb-9">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Why I built it</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">Real-world BOMs are rarely clean database records. A row may mix a manufacturer, MPN, package, description, and quantity; naming conventions vary, fields go missing, and a search result is not automatically the right part.</p>
    <p>The prototype explores a more reviewable workflow: structure the input first, search for candidates second, and keep uncertain results visible for human review instead of presenting every result as a confirmed match.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-9">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Try the demo</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li>Open the demo and choose one of the prepared BOM scenarios.</li>
      <li>Run the normalization flow and inspect the structured BOM table.</li>
      <li>Review row-level results and use supplier candidate lookup where available.</li>
      <li>Inspect candidate details before treating a result as a possible component choice.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="alert mt-4">
      <span class="text-sm">The demo is designed for exploration. Its prepared scenarios and simulated progress make the workflow easy to inspect without uploading customer BOMs or exposing private supplier credentials.</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-9">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">How it works</h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-4 gap-2 text-center">
      <div class="card bg-base-200 p-3">
        <div class="text-xs uppercase opacity-60">01 · Input</div>
        <div class="font-semibold mt-1">Browser UI</div>
        <div class="text-xs opacity-70 mt-1">Prepared BOM scenarios and field selection</div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center opacity-50">→</div>
      <div class="card bg-base-200 p-3">
        <div class="text-xs uppercase opacity-60">02 · API</div>
        <div class="font-semibold mt-1">Cloudflare Worker</div>
        <div class="text-xs opacity-70 mt-1">Demo routes and workflow orchestration</div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center opacity-50">→</div>
      <div class="card bg-base-200 p-3">
        <div class="text-xs uppercase opacity-60">03 · Normalize</div>
        <div class="font-semibold mt-1">Prepared fixtures</div>
        <div class="text-xs opacity-70 mt-1">Structured sample output and review states</div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center opacity-50">→</div>
      <div class="card bg-base-200 p-3">
        <div class="text-xs uppercase opacity-60">04 · Search</div>
        <div class="font-semibold mt-1">Mouser service binding</div>
        <div class="text-xs opacity-70 mt-1">Keyword-based supplier candidates</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs opacity-60 mt-3">This describes the current demo implementation, not a production-grade AI sourcing architecture.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-9">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">What is actually implemented</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="table table-zebra">
        <thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Current behavior</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Demo interface</td><td>Deployed browser-based BOM workspace with prepared scenarios and editable review controls.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Normalization</td><td>Uses prepared demo fixtures and simulated progress states; it is not arbitrary-file or general-purpose LLM parsing.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Supplier lookup</td><td>Connects keyword search through a Mouser service binding and returns candidate products.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Deployment</td><td>Runs as a separate Cloudflare Worker named <code>ai-bom-demo</code>, isolated from the production source branch.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-9">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Design decisions</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Separate parsing from matching.</strong> A normalized row is a search-ready input, not proof that a component has been identified correctly.</li>
      <li><strong>Keep uncertain outcomes reviewable.</strong> Candidate results should be inspected rather than silently promoted to exact matches.</li>
      <li><strong>Isolate the demo environment.</strong> The portfolio build has its own Worker configuration and does not deploy by syncing GitHub source alone.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-9">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Scope and limitations</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li>No arbitrary BOM file upload or general-purpose LLM extraction in the current release.</li>
      <li>Normalization output is based on prepared demo data; progress animation is simulated.</li>
      <li>Supplier keyword results are candidates, not guaranteed exact matches or verified sourcing recommendations.</li>
      <li>The demo does not guarantee live stock, lead time, order availability, or quote accuracy.</li>
      <li>Quantities in the 20-row sample scenario are illustrative demo values, not customer data.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="border-t border-base-300 pt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://ai-bom-demo.buwygfimb.workers.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Try the Demo ↗</a>
    <a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://github.com/wantosleep3/ai-bom-Copilot" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Source Code ↗</a>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
